invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select uses the mask it computed, with no volatile pointer
  between the computation and the use, so the compiler knows the mask is
  all ones at the entry whose position is the digit and zero elsewhere.
  clang for x86-64 then compiles the scan to a comparison of the two
  positions, a branch on it and a read of the one entry that matched:
  both follow a digit of the private exponent. Every byte still comes out
  the same, so the vectors and the equivalence test pass. The file's
  count of conditional branches is no reliable sign of it: the comparison
  adds one branch on the x86-64 spec, which a branch gained or lost
  elsewhere in the file can hide, and none on the arm64 spec, where the
  select is a csel. inv-16-rsa-table-read refuses a mask in table_select
  that is taken straight from mask_of_bit.

--- old
        *hidden = mask_of_bit(differ ^ 1);
        uint64_t mask = *hidden;
--- new
        uint64_t mask = mask_of_bit(differ ^ 1);
